{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "8294734",
      "title": "Adding a Reusable Modal Component with useEffect",
      "sourceHash": "6bbac5774316c6fa13cdb530e4fb23be5a4459eaca5c9994df3792dd86fc4878",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0,
          "end": 2.64,
          "en": "So let's make sure this cart button here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.64,
          "end": 5.64,
          "en": "opens up a modal that shows us the cart details.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.64,
          "end": 8.34,
          "en": "And for that of course we'll need a modal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.34,
          "end": 13.11,
          "en": "a component that opens as an overlay on the screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.11,
          "end": 18.11,
          "en": "and I'll build that as a standalone reusable UI component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.81,
          "end": 20.97,
          "en": "so that we could also use the modal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.97,
          "end": 22.83,
          "en": "in other places of the app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.83,
          "end": 26.913,
          "en": "And we will indeed also use it in one other place later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.96,
          "end": 30.963,
          "en": "So I'll add my modal JSX file here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.19,
          "end": 37.19,
          "en": "and in there I want to export my modal component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 39.99,
          "end": 43.08,
          "en": "Now in this modal component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 43.08,
          "end": 46.71,
          "en": "I want a return built-in dialogue element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 46.71,
          "end": 49.8,
          "en": "which is great for displaying overlays like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 49.8,
          "end": 53.31,
          "en": "because it handles a lot of the complexity for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 53.31,
          "end": 55.17,
          "en": "But I wanna output it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 55.17,
          "end": 59.7,
          "en": "with help of that portal feature React offers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 59.7,
          "end": 62.94,
          "en": "so that we can use this modal component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 62.94,
          "end": 66.33,
          "en": "from anywhere in our component tree.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 66.33,
          "end": 69.6,
          "en": "But we'll always inject the dialogue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 69.6,
          "end": 74.6,
          "en": "when it's visible in a specific area of the Real DOM",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 74.76,
          "end": 77.85300000000001,
          "en": "that we as a developer control upfront.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 79.11,
          "end": 82.74,
          "en": "And I wanna inject it into this div here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 82.74,
          "end": 85.623,
          "en": "sorry, this div here, with an idea of modal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 86.49,
          "end": 90.36,
          "en": "That's where I wanna inject those dialogue elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 90.36,
          "end": 94.263,
          "en": "when we create and open them with the modal component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 95.31,
          "end": 97.14,
          "en": "And of course, that's exactly what",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 97.14,
          "end": 98.91,
          "en": "that portal feature is for,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 98.91,
          "end": 101.28,
          "en": "about which you learned in the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 101.28,
          "end": 104.07,
          "en": "We can easily create such a portal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 104.07,
          "end": 106.89,
          "en": "with help of the create portal function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 106.89,
          "end": 109.233,
          "en": "that's imported from React-dom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 110.82,
          "end": 115.22999999999999,
          "en": "And you then simply return, not the dialogue element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 115.22999999999999,
          "end": 118.83,
          "en": "but instead a call to React portal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 118.83,
          "end": 123.83,
          "en": "where the JSX content that should be portaled somewhere else",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 124.29,
          "end": 127.38,
          "en": "and that should be rendered by this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 127.38,
          "end": 131.796,
          "en": "is passed as a first argument to create portal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 131.796,
          "end": 135.93,
          "en": "And then the second argument is some code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 135.93,
          "end": 139.65,
          "en": "that selects an element in the Real DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 139.65,
          "end": 143.57999999999998,
          "en": "And here I'll use document getElementById for that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 143.57999999999998,
          "end": 147.183,
          "en": "to select the element with an idea of modal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 148.23,
          "end": 150.753,
          "en": "which will of course be that div here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 152.4,
          "end": 155.97,
          "en": "So that's how we can create such a portal here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 155.97,
          "end": 160.11,
          "en": "Now my idea with this modal component then,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 160.11,
          "end": 163.32,
          "en": "essentially is that it can be wrapped",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 163.32,
          "end": 166.2,
          "en": "around any content of our choice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 166.2,
          "end": 168.903,
          "en": "to put that content into the dialogue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 169.86,
          "end": 173.64,
          "en": "And therefore I'll accept and destructure the children prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 173.64,
          "end": 176.913,
          "en": "and pass that between the dialogue elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 178.2,
          "end": 181.32,
          "en": "In addition here, I wanna make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 181.32,
          "end": 185.58,
          "en": "that this modal component can be controlled",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 185.58,
          "end": 188.85,
          "en": "with help of an open prop that can be set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 188.85,
          "end": 190.92,
          "en": "on my custom modal component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 190.92,
          "end": 194.343,
          "en": "that should control whether the dialogue is open or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 195.66,
          "end": 199.98,
          "en": "Now the built in dialogue element also has an open attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 199.98,
          "end": 202.68,
          "en": "that can be set, and theoretically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 202.68,
          "end": 206.16,
          "en": "we could therefore simply forward that open prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 206.16,
          "end": 208.263,
          "en": "to the open prop of the dialogue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 209.46,
          "end": 213.84,
          "en": "But if we do that, we miss out on certain features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 213.84,
          "end": 216.9,
          "en": "And most importantly, this dialogue element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 216.9,
          "end": 219.36,
          "en": "when opened programmatically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 219.36,
          "end": 222.32999999999998,
          "en": "so not by setting this open prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 222.32999999999998,
          "end": 224.97,
          "en": "automatically displays a backdrop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 224.97,
          "end": 227.73,
          "en": "So a little area behind the overlay",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 227.73,
          "end": 231.57,
          "en": "that can be used to gray out the other content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 231.57,
          "end": 233.73,
          "en": "and to overlay the other content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 233.73,
          "end": 235.74,
          "en": "so that we can't interact with it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 235.74,
          "end": 238.41,
          "en": "whilst the dialogue is open.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 238.41,
          "end": 240.63,
          "en": "And that's why I don't wanna open it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 240.63,
          "end": 242.49,
          "en": "by setting the open prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 242.49,
          "end": 245.16,
          "en": "But why instead I want to open the dialogue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 245.16,
          "end": 247.11,
          "en": "programmatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 247.11,
          "end": 249.3,
          "en": "Now one way of achieving this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 249.3,
          "end": 251.61,
          "en": "as you learned earlier in the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 251.61,
          "end": 255.75,
          "en": "would be to use a ref, or a forward ref,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 255.75,
          "end": 259.2,
          "en": "depending on which React version you are using,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 259.2,
          "end": 263.88,
          "en": "to allow other components to interact with this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 263.88,
          "end": 267.03,
          "en": "So to expose some functions, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 267.03,
          "end": 270.12,
          "en": "that can be called by other components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 270.12,
          "end": 271.86,
          "en": "And whilst this would work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 271.86,
          "end": 273.93,
          "en": "I'll take a different route here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 273.93,
          "end": 277.5,
          "en": "I'll use useEffect here also to, again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 277.5,
          "end": 281.04,
          "en": "practice working with that to, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 281.04,
          "end": 284.31,
          "en": "interact with that native dialogue element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 284.31,
          "end": 287.223,
          "en": "whenever the open prop value changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 288.72,
          "end": 293.1,
          "en": "So I'll pass open as a dependency to this dependencies array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 293.1,
          "end": 295.74,
          "en": "so that this effect function will rerun",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 295.74,
          "end": 297.389,
          "en": "whenever open changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 297.389,
          "end": 300.24,
          "en": "And then in this effect function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 300.24,
          "end": 302.433,
          "en": "I'll then check if open is true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 303.39,
          "end": 306.84,
          "en": "And if it is true, I want to open this dialogue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 306.84,
          "end": 307.953,
          "en": "programmatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 308.88,
          "end": 313.17,
          "en": "To do this, we need to get access to the dialogue element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 313.17,
          "end": 316.41,
          "en": "And as you learned, that's something which we can do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 316.41,
          "end": 317.823,
          "en": "with help of refs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 318.69,
          "end": 321.87,
          "en": "We can use the built-in useRef hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 321.87,
          "end": 325.889,
          "en": "by importing it from React, and by then calling useRef,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 325.889,
          "end": 330,
          "en": "and then connect this dialogue Ref here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 330,
          "end": 332.28,
          "en": "to the built-in dialogue element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 332.28,
          "end": 336.69,
          "en": "through the built-in Ref prop like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 336.69,
          "end": 339.18,
          "en": "Now, inside of this effect function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 339.18,
          "end": 344.18,
          "en": "inside of this if block, so only if open is true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 344.73,
          "end": 347.28,
          "en": "we can use this dialogue Ref",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 347.28,
          "end": 351.75,
          "en": "to call showModal, which is the built in method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 351.75,
          "end": 356.13,
          "en": "that can be executed on this dialogue object in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 356.13,
          "end": 359.223,
          "en": "to show it, to open it programmatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 360.54,
          "end": 363.753,
          "en": "And we'll take care about closing it later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 364.83,
          "end": 367.05,
          "en": "To finish up this modal component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 367.05,
          "end": 369.39,
          "en": "and this dialogue element for now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 369.39,
          "end": 372.75,
          "en": "I'll also add the className prop here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 372.75,
          "end": 377.01,
          "en": "to add a class of modal to this dialogue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 377.01,
          "end": 380.299,
          "en": "though I actually want to make this a bit more dynamic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 380.299,
          "end": 383.85,
          "en": "And I wanna make sure that this modal component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 383.85,
          "end": 388.23,
          "en": "can also be styled from outside this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 388.23,
          "end": 391.83,
          "en": "so that other components can also set a className prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 391.83,
          "end": 393.93,
          "en": "on this modal component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 393.93,
          "end": 397.98,
          "en": "and this value then is merged with this modal class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 397.98,
          "end": 399.753,
          "en": "that should always be applied.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 402.06,
          "end": 404.19,
          "en": "And this can be achieved by setting className",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 404.19,
          "end": 406.08,
          "en": "to a dynamic value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 406.08,
          "end": 409.08,
          "en": "which in the end is a template literal string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 409.08,
          "end": 412.92,
          "en": "where I always have the hard coded modal class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 412.92,
          "end": 415.74,
          "en": "and I then also inject the class name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 415.74,
          "end": 417.693,
          "en": "I might be receiving in addition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 418.65,
          "end": 421.26,
          "en": "Now theoretically this could then lead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 421.26,
          "end": 425.13,
          "en": "to undefined being added as a className",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 425.13,
          "end": 427.05,
          "en": "if className is not set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 427.05,
          "end": 429.18,
          "en": "And therefore I'll give this a default value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 429.18,
          "end": 432.36,
          "en": "of an empty string, so that we basically don't add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 432.36,
          "end": 437.013,
          "en": "any text here if className should not be set from outside.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 438.99,
          "end": 443.01,
          "en": "And that's therefore it for this modal component for now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 443.01,
          "end": 447.093,
          "en": "As a next step, we can use it to output some cart details.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}